id: pm-ado-sdk-scalar-normalization
title: Expose SDK assignment mutation normalization
description: "SDK 2026.10.23 has no public pure assignment-mutation normalizer. sdk/lifecycle/legacy-none-tokens.d.ts:65 declares isLegacyNoneToken(value: string | undefined), but that internal module is absent from package exports; root and sdk/runtime namespaces expose neither isLegacyNoneToken nor normalizeAssigneeMutationInput. Public toNonEmptyImportString handles trimming; normalizeItemMetadata preserves literal assignee strings, whereas native commitItemMutations interprets assignment none/null as clear. previewItemMutations returns ItemMutationPreviewValidation only, without canonical field results; transaction/settings/events/history APIs do not provide a pure equivalent. Open upstream searches normalize assignee and isLegacyNoneToken SDK found no matching issue. Adapter uses the SDK trim primitive plus one centralized clear-token predicate, verified against actual native writes. Title/description none/null remain literal. Missing public export: isLegacyNoneToken or an SDK normalizeAssigneeMutationInput with explicit scalar clear semantics. Orchestrator verifies and files upstream."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[1]: sdk-gap
created_at: "2026-10-27T09:56:19.176Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T10:22:56.823Z"
author: codex-agent
parent: pm-ado-sdk-adoption
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T10:22:56.796Z",codex-agent,"Native SDK write-oracle verification passed: assignment none/null clears while title/description none/null remain literal; whitespace and Unicode are preserved exactly where native writes preserve them. The pure missing assignment clear-token export is the only new SDK API gap; original audit replacements remain implemented. The shared normalizer module measured 100% lines, branches and functions in the focused native-tracker run."
